From 30879fd327f2abdb073a7a4e93102a6a5f939e1c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Morinaga <me@gustavomorinaga.dev>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:39:35 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: the frame's jitter is the last record's;
 per-object motion (opt-in)

The draws of a frame carry the jitter the camera made a frame earlier
(their own motion on still scenes agrees with the camera's to 0.01 px
only so), while the view-projection is the frame's own: DLSS and FSR now
get that jitter, and the motion pass corrects for it.

PS3RECOMP_TEMPORAL_OBJECT_MOTION=1: draws into the scene use a velocity
variant of their pipeline. Its vertex program runs again on the
constants the same draw had last frame (VPPrev, binding 2), found by the
engine's draw key (program, count, topology; set_draw_key), the
material, and the closest constants among draws of that key, and its
pixel program writes the difference into one more target. The motion
pass takes it, less the jitter change, where it is within 6% of the
frame of the camera's motion. Off by default: some draws still pair
with the wrong instance.

PS3RECOMP_VK_DUMP_PRESENTS=<first>,<count> dumps a run of presents, and
the temporal dump writes the motion and velocity images too.

